# ATO project safeguards

Apply only in `ai-enabled-ato`. Read the current root `AGENTS.md` first.
Use the project `ato-ssp-workflow` skill for evidence, SSP drafting, contextual
assistance, review and exports. Use installed global `agentic-security-workflows`
with its SSP-authoring reference for shared workflow principles.

- Keep pinned authority/profile/version and current-profile scope. Content
  completion and review establish neither control effectiveness nor authorization.
- Private conversations cannot alter canonical SSP content without an approved
  proposal. Preserve exact-revision approval, stale/dirty checks and human edits.
- Evidence changes invalidate the documented dependent facts/proposals/reviews;
  source-link saves do not themselves call a model. Keep control re-analysis scoped.
- Export the exact saved revision with provenance and limits. Preserve earlier
  exports/history; exporting does not introduce a separate SSP approval requirement.
- GitHub Actions is disabled for this app by user instruction. Use local checks;
  do not initiate GitHub work, enable/maintain workflows or remediate inactive
  workflow findings unless the user explicitly requests it. Preserve production
  qualification and application-security requirements.

Current app documents and the packaged full AGENTS snapshot identify the detailed
contracts. These instructions add no new authorization workflow or execution scope.
